9,Shwai language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/shwai_language,"Unlike many Niger-Congo languages in the region, Shwai lacks advanced tongue root (ATR) harmony, allowing non-harmonic co-occurrences within words; for instance, /i/ and /ɪ/ contrast in viði 'cut hair' and ðixɪ 'thorn', while mid-vowel alternates appear in forms like oɽɛl 'piece of stone'.",Shwai,Niger-Congo
